 "source_type": "instagram",
 "source_url": "https://www.instagram.com/reel/DZ5Q5Qmp1mz/",
 "title": "Stop Romanticising Struggle",
 "topic": "mindset",
 "summary": "The creator argues that people should use every unfair advantage they have instead of romanticising unnecessary hardship. She states that the goal is to build a good life rather than prove how much pain one can endure.",
 "key_points": [
  "Use every unfair advantage you have in life, whether it is looks, genetics, connections, parents, or money.",
  "There is nothing noble about making your life harder just to call yourself an underdog.",
  "Success does not only count if it comes from suffering, and the goal is not to prove how much pain you can endure.",
  "Pretending an advantage does not exist does not make you humble; it just makes you inefficient.",
  "People who achieve extraordinary things rarely spend time apologizing for their advantages; they acknowledge and use them.",
  "The purpose of an advantage is not to feel guilty, but to help yourself go further because of it."
 ],
 "content": "Instagram reel/post by unfilterxd22. Text / caption: nobody’s giving out brownie points for selecting the harder route. Transcript: I don't know who needs to hear this, but use every unfair advantage you have in life. Your looks, your genetics, your connections, your parents, money, whatever it is. Use it, because there's nothing noble about making your life harder just to call yourself an underdog. Some people may act like success only counts if it comes from suffering, as if the goal is to prove how much pain you can endure. It's not. The goal is to build a good life, right? If you've been given an advantage, pretending it doesn't exist doesn't make you humble, it just makes you inefficient. The people who achieve extraordinary things rarely spend their time apologizing for their advantages. They acknowledge them and use them. Remember that the purpose of an advantage is not to feel guilty about it, it is to help yourself go further because of it.",
